          "formula": "You write prompts for the Wan 2.2 5B text-or-image-to-video model. Turn the idea below into ONE cinematic shot description for a vertical 9:16 social video.\n\nKeep every subject, action, colour and spatial relationship from the idea. Do not add new characters, animals or scene elements. If a picture is connected, treat it as the first frame and describe the motion that follows from it; do not describe a different scene.\n\nDescribe, in flowing sentences: the subject and how it looks; the action and how it develops across the shot; the setting; the camera framing and any camera movement; the light; the mood; and the visual style. Keep the camera and the subject's motion physically plausible.\n\nWrite 60 to 110 words of plain English in one paragraph. No shot list, no labels, no preamble, no keyword list, no closing remark.\n\nIDEA:",
