      "title": "Quality helpers - how they work",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Quality helpers (optional)\n\nThese nodes add two local passes with **Qwen3-VL 4B**: `qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors` (5.24 GB, Apache 2.0). It is part of the shorts catalog and lives in `models/text_encoders`. Install it with `setup --short --install`.\n\n**1. Your idea -> Prompt enhancer -> prompt encoder.** Edit the idea in **Your idea**. The enhancer rewrites it for this workflow's model, using the source picture when one is connected, and feeds the positive prompt encoder. To use your idea unchanged, select the enhancer and press **Ctrl+B** (bypass); the idea passes straight through to the encoder.\n\n**2. Generated media -> Post writer.** After the final frames are decoded, the post writer looks at them and writes a caption, hashtags, and alt text. The result appears in **Post copy preview** and is saved to `output/Shorts/wan5b-post.txt` while the workflow is open in the browser. A headless API run does not write the file. Running again replaces the file.\n\nThe post writer reads the decoded Wan 5B frames.\n\nBoth nodes load the model when they run and free it afterwards (**Free VRAM** is on). Expect a few extra seconds on the first run and after each pass. If VRAM is tight, bypass the post writer and use `shorts-post.sh` for copy instead.\n\nNeeds the **ComfyUI-Pixaroma** custom node pack (Manager -> Install Missing Custom Nodes).\n"
      ]
    }
  ],
